    scoringRules: {
      summary: 'Melded cards score points: aces and wild cards are typically worth 100 points each (or 200 when aces are wild); other picture cards and tens are 10 points; numeral cards 2–9 are 5 points. Unmelded cards left in hand at the end of a hand count against the player, and going out may award a bonus. Target score is often 5000, but many groups use 1500, 2000, 2200, 2500, 2800 or 10000.',
      winCondition: 'Be the first player to reach the target score (often 5000) by melding sets and runs and going out; opponents add deadwood to your score.',
